          "end": 193.53,
          "en": "But, let's say, if you want to store a bunch of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 193.53,
          "end": 195.12,
          "en": "how will you work with that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 195.12,
          "end": 197.22,
          "en": "And when it comes to data structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 197.22,
          "end": 199.38,
          "en": "how will you store this data in a proper way?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 199.38,
          "end": 200.213,
          "en": "See what happens is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 200.213,
          "end": 202.02,
          "en": "when you talk about primitive types as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 202.02,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "every type will have a way to store data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "Of course, that's why we're getting them, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 209.43,
          "en": "So example, if you are getting a variable called num.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 209.43,
          "end": 212.28,
          "en": "Now, let's say this num is of type integer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 212.28,
          "end": 214.05,
          "en": "and then you are storing a value to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 214.05,
          "end": 215.22,
          "en": "Now with this variable num,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 215.22,
          "end": 217.47,
          "en": "you can perform operations as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 219.03,
          "en": "Now, what are the options you can do within integer?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 219.03,
          "end": 219.99,
          "en": "You can add two values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 219.99,
          "end": 221.07,
          "en": "you can subtract two values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 221.07,
          "end": 222.63,
          "en": "you can divide, multiply.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 225.99,
          "en": "So you can perform those operations on the number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 225.99,
          "end": 227.37,
          "en": "But, let's say, you have a string there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 228.57,
          "en": "Now with string, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 228.57,
          "end": 229.95,
          "en": "you will not be adding two string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "That doesn't make sense, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 232.44,
          "en": "Why you will add two names?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 232.44,
          "end": 233.28,
          "en": "Let's say, Navin and Kiran,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 233.28,
          "end": 234.48,
          "en": "you will get a new name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 234.48,
          "end": 236.25,
          "en": "Okay, a lot of parents are doing that for their kids,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 237.51,
          "en": "but that's not the idea here, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 237.51,
          "end": 238.71,
          "en": "We can't add a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 238.71,
          "end": 240.3,
          "en": "we cannot subtract strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 240.3,
          "end": 241.95,
          "en": "But yes, with string you can do something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 241.95,
          "end": 244.2,
          "en": "Maybe you want to see the size of a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 244.2,
          "end": 246.72,
          "en": "maybe you want to concatenate two strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 246.72,
          "end": 248.07,
          "en": "maybe you want to cut two strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
